=== chromium: desktop: unencrypted ===
0.0.0.0:1 is not encrypted: the password and everything prigh sends would cross the network in the clear, and anyone on the way could run commands on this computer. Use the backend's HTTPS address (wss://host/ws, behind a TLS reverse proxy), or an SSH tunnel (ssh -L 7790:localhost:7790 host, then 127.0.0.1:<PORT>). Connect anyway only on a network you trust.
button: Connect without encryption
